1
00:00:00,009 --> 00:00:05,009
STC MINI HACKATHON 2026 · DISASTER RECOVERY · DRY RUN · Find gaps in your flood plan before you need it. · A short flood-plan rehearsal for a household, a kedai or a community.

2
00:00:05,732 --> 00:00:10,232
Five topics: warnings, evacuation, people, communication and essentials.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,429
For this demo, a fictional sample plan. Your own plan stays separate.

4
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:19,551
Each card is a disruption. Would your backup still work? Choose, then explain why.

5
00:00:19,554 --> 00:00:24,457
No backup for transport: the plan has a gap, and the water rises.

6
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,345
Now the shared failure.

7
00:00:28,347 --> 00:00:33,347
First choice WhatsApp, backup Telegram. Two apps, one mobile network.

8
00:00:33,349 --> 00:00:40,913
If the network goes down, both go down. That is not really a backup.

9
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:46,317
The review: gaps found, things to check, and backups named.

10
00:00:46,322 --> 00:00:51,226
Every topic gets its own water level and plain-language next step.

11
00:00:51,228 --> 00:00:56,611
Communication: gap found. Patch it.

12
00:00:56,613 --> 00:01:01,818
Patch: a fallback that does not need the phone network at all.

13
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:06,055
Then rehearse again.

14
00:01:06,057 --> 00:01:18,879
The changed answer is flagged: reassess this scenario.

15
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,788
Reassessed.

16
00:01:21,789 --> 00:01:27,290
Before and after: Communication went from gap found to backup named.

17
00:01:27,292 --> 00:01:32,396
The other gaps stay visible. It is a rehearsal, not a safety rating.

18
00:01:32,398 --> 00:01:37,803
For real warnings and shelters: official Malaysian sources, linked, never copied.

19
00:01:37,805 --> 00:01:41,805
Print it for the fridge. It works offline, with no login, on any phone.

20
00:01:41,808 --> 00:01:47,808
DRY RUN · A warning tells you danger is coming. · Dry Run shows which part of your plan fails when it arrives. · stc-mini-hackathon-2026.vercel.app
